DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The wwccssccaasseeccmmpp() function is the wide‐character equivalent of the  ssttrr‐‐
       ccaasseeccmmpp(3)  function.  It compares the wide‐character string pointed to
       by _s_1 and the wide‐character string pointed to  by  _s_2,  ignoring  case
       differences (ttoowwuuppppeerr(3), ttoowwlloowweerr(3)).

       The wwccssnnccaasseeccmmpp() function is similar (the wide‐character equivalent of
       ssttrrnnccaasseeccmmpp(3)), except that it compares no more than _n wide characters
       of _s_1 and _s_2.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The  wwccssccaasseeccmmpp()  and  wwccssnnccaasseeccmmpp()  functions return an integer less
       than, equal to, or greater than zero if _s_1  is,  after  ignoring  case,
       found to be less than, to match, or be greater than _s_2, respectively.

